Pi-hole on FenrirOS
===================

Pi-hole's installer (basic-install.sh) is not used and not shipped. The
pieces are installed inert, in upstream's places:
  /usr/bin/pihole-FTL        the FTL daemon (DNS/DHCP, API, web server)
  /usr/bin/pihole            the command; its scripts in /opt/pihole
  /var/www/html/admin        the web interface (served by FTL itself)
  /usr/share/pihole/core     the core scripts' data (upstream's /etc/.pihole)
Nothing runs, no configuration, gravity database or password exists yet.
`pihole -up`, `repair`, `uninstall` and `checkout` are disabled: apk
manages Pi-hole.

Setup
  1. Free port 53: nothing else may serve DNS on this host (dnsmasq, unbound,
     a local resolver).
  2. Start FTL once so that it writes /etc/pihole/pihole.toml, or write it
     with `pihole-FTL --config <key> <value>`, e.g.
         pihole-FTL --config dns.upstreams '["9.9.9.9"]'
         pihole-FTL --config dns.interface eth0
  3. SET A PASSWORD before anything else can reach the web interface or the
     API: with no password Pi-hole asks for none.
         pihole setpassword
  4. dinitctl enable pihole-FTL
  5. Add block lists (web interface: Lists) and build the gravity database:
         pihole -g
  The web interface is at http://<host>/admin (FTL's own web server, ports
  80 and 443; webserver.port in pihole.toml).

Periodic jobs
  Upstream runs `pihole updateGravity` weekly and `pihole updatechecker`
  daily from cron (updatechecker asks GitHub for new versions). An example
  is /usr/share/doc/pi-hole/pihole.cron (crond: cronie); copy it to
  /etc/cron.d/pihole if you want them.

Telemetry: Pi-hole has none. `pihole -d` (debug log) only uploads when you
answer yes to its question.
